  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_039: multimodal, scgpt+imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted → acc 0.52), the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal fusion is actually contributing meaningful signal over a single-modality baseline. Config_001 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, transformer) is the natural RNA-only counterpart that keeps the same RNA encoder and aggregation strategy, isolating the effect of the image modality. If RNA alone performs comparably (~0.50-0.52), the search can focus on refining the RNA pipeline or testing simpler image encoders; if it performs substantially worse, it confirms the value of multimodal fusion and justifies further exploration of fusion strategies and image encoders. This is the highest-information experiment at this stage because it partitions the 8 remaining experiments between two very different search strategies (optimize multimodal fusion vs. optimize single-modality model), and the answer is unlikely to be resolved by tweaking secondary knobs like fusion type or aggregation."
}

